 Let us denote the distance travelled towards east by positive sign. So, the distances towards west would be denoted by negative sign. \textcolor{red}{Additionally, knowing that 1 km = 1000 meters, we can convert these distances into meters if necessary.}

Thus, the distance of Satpal from the point P would be:
\[
\frac{2}{3} + \left(-\frac{5}{7}\right) = \frac{2}{3} + \left(-\frac{12}{7}\right) = \frac{2 \times 7}{3 \times 7} + \left(-\frac{12 \times 3}{7 \times 3}\right)
\]
\[
= \frac{14 - 36}{21} = -\frac{22}{21} = -\frac{1}{21}
\]

Since it is negative, it means Satpal is at a distance \( \frac{1}{21} \) km towards west of P. \textcolor{red}{Interestingly, if we convert this distance to meters, it would be approximately 47.62 meters.}

